# circuit.numos — Circuit (APP 13 · CircuitCoreApp) capture script for paadweb.
#
# The three shots this file owns (tests/emulator/scripts/screenshots/README.md):
#   1. /assets/img/apps/circuit-1.webp — edit mode, mid-build (supply→resistor→
#      transistor, coin cell→AND→7-segment, programmable block at the bottom)
#   2. /assets/img/apps/circuit-2.webp — simulation running (heatmap, dual-trace
#      scope, current arrows, multimeter reading)
#   3. /assets/img/apps/circuit-3.webp — the programmable block's editor open
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# STATUS: 0 of the 3 shots are capturable on this build. CircuitCoreApp is NOT
# compiled into the emulator, so there is no Circuit screen to reach, to assert
# on, or to capture. Evidence (all from this repo / this exact binary):
#   * platformio.ini [env:emulator_pc] build_src_filter is a per-file whitelist;
#     it lists apps one by one and has NO +<apps/CircuitCoreApp.cpp>, and
#     C:/.piobuild/numOS/emulator_pc/src/apps/ has no CircuitCoreApp.o.
#   * src/hal/NativeHal.cpp:1338 launchApp() has no case 13 — it prints
#     "[APP] App 13 no implementada en simulador" and leaves the mode alone.
#   * NativeHal.cpp:2229 scriptAppNameToId() has no "circuit" slug, so a script
#     containing `open_app circuit` fails to LOAD (reproduced on this binary,
#     exit 2):
#       [SCRIPT] <file>:3: open_app: app no lanzable
#         (Calculation|Grapher|Statistics|Probability|Sequences|Regression|
#          Settings|MathShowcase|MathVisual|GameBoy|Notes|AI)
#   * NativeHal.cpp:2189 canonicalAppName() has no "Circuit", so `assert_app
#     Circuit` would likewise fail to load with exit 2.
#   * The binary itself carries no CircuitCoreApp string at all (no "Resistor",
#     "Multimeter", "7-Segment", ... — only the launcher card label "Circuit").
#
# The launcher CARD does exist (MainMenu.cpp:126, {13, "Circuit", ...}), so this
# script does what IS provable: focus that card, activate it, and assert that
# the emulator keeps the launcher — i.e. machine-check the dead card. It writes
# no screenshot: a launcher frame must never land on circuit-1/2/3.webp.
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# INTENDED CAPTURE WALK — UNVERIFIED, NOT EXECUTED (kept for the rebuild once
# app 13 is added to the emulator whitelist + NativeHal routing). Traced from
# src/apps/CircuitCoreApp.cpp only; no line of it has ever run, and three
# source-level hazards are known (see the report's NOTES):
#   SHOT 1 (edit mode): begin() starts focus=GRID, cursor=(100,80), tool=RES
#     (CircuitCoreApp.cpp:156-163). AC → toolbar, arrows walk the 3x10 toolbar
#     (page 0 RES..DIO, page 1 LDR..7SG, page 2 AND..RUN; handleKeyToolbar
#     :578), ENTER selects and returns focus to GRID, ENTER in GRID places
#     (handleKeyGrid:497 → placeComponent:633). Plan: MCU at (100,80) bottom
#     row; row y=20: VCC(40) w w RES(100) w w NPN(160); row y=40: 3V(40) w w
#     AND(100) w w 7SG(160); wires via the WIRE tool (page0 idx5).
#     assert_app Circuit · assert_theme numos
#     # screenshot out/shots-circuit-1.ppm   (NOT RUN — app unreachable)
#   SHOT 2 (simulation): RUN (page2 idx9, ENTER toggles startSimulation:775 and
#     leaves focus on the toolbar → DOWN back to GRID); F2 toggles the voltage
#     heatmap only while running (:548); ENTER on a component arms scope Ch1,
#     ENTER on a second component arms Ch2 (:497-522, drawScope:1032);
#     AC → MTR (page2 idx8) → ENTER probes the multimeter (probeMultimeter:1294);
#     drawCurrentArrows/drawMultimeter/drawVoltageHeatmap all gate on
#     _simRunning (onDraw:964-1008). Note: in SIM the cursor only moves with
#     LEFT/RIGHT — UP/DOWN are pot/sensor/timebase (handleKeyGrid:465-487).
#     assert_app Circuit · assert_theme numos
#     # screenshot out/shots-circuit-2.ppm   (NOT RUN — app unreachable)
#   SHOT 3 (MCU editor): stop the sim (RUN again), EDIT mode, cursor on the MCU,
#     ENTER → openIDE() (:527-528, :1934). The overlay prefills the textarea
#     with "void setup(){\n}\nvoid loop(){\n}" (:1966) — that is a C skeleton,
#     NOT Lua, and handleKeyIDE (:2022) accepts only digits, ENTER, F4 and AC,
#     so no Lua line can be typed from a .numos script.
#     assert_app Circuit · assert_theme numos
#     # screenshot out/shots-circuit-3.ppm   (NOT RUN — app unreachable)
#
# Run:
#   program --headless --deterministic \
#       --script tests/emulator/scripts/screenshots/circuit.numos \
#       --fs-root tests/emulator/fs --frames 1400 --quiet
# Exit codes: 0 ok · 2 script/parse error · 3 screenshot error · 4 assertion failure.

log "circuit: waiting for splash -> launcher"
wait 200
assert_app Menu
assert_theme numos

# The launcher grid is 3 columns wide (menu_nav_parity.numos), so card id 13
# (Circuit) is row 4, column 1. Four DOWNs keep the column, one RIGHT lands on it.
key down
key down
key down
key down
key right
assert_menu_focus Circuit

# Activate the card. launchApp(13) is unimplemented in the emulator, so the
# launcher must stay active — this assert is the machine check that app 13 is a
# dead card on THIS build. (If it ever FAILS, routing was added: then rebuild
# the walk above, add `open_app circuit` + `assert_app Circuit`, and capture.)
key enter
wait 60
assert_app Menu
assert_theme numos

log "circuit: card id 13 focused and activated; emulator kept the launcher"
log "circuit: 0 of 3 shots captured — CircuitCoreApp is not in the emulator build"
